Chapter: Bacnet

 BACnet/IP (ANSI/ASHRAE 135), the building-automation protocol for HVAC,
 lighting, access control, and metering in commercial buildings. A
 message is a BVLC header (0x81, function, two-byte length) wrapping an
 NPDU (network layer) and an APDU (application layer). The APDU encodes
 objects and properties with tagged data: a context tag is
 (tag-number << 4) | 0x08 | length, an object identifier packs a 10-bit
 type and a 22-bit inst into four bytes. This chapter builds a
 confirmed ReadProperty request; more services follow the same tag
 machinery.

Section: Object Types

  bacnet-obj-analog-input : Integer = 0
  bacnet-obj-analog-output : Integer = 1
  bacnet-obj-analog-value : Integer = 2
  bacnet-obj-binary-input : Integer = 3
  bacnet-obj-binary-output : Integer = 4
  bacnet-obj-binary-value : Integer = 5
  bacnet-obj-device : Integer = 8
  bacnet-obj-multi-state-value : Integer = 19

Section: Property Identifiers

  bacnet-prop-description : Integer = 28
  bacnet-prop-object-name : Integer = 77
  bacnet-prop-object-type : Integer = 79
  bacnet-prop-present-value : Integer = 85
  bacnet-prop-status-flags : Integer = 111
  bacnet-prop-units : Integer = 117

Section: Services and BVLC

  bacnet-svc-read-property : Integer = 12
  bacnet-svc-read-property-multiple : Integer = 14
  bacnet-svc-write-property : Integer = 15

  bacnet-bvlc-original-unicast : Integer = #0A
  bacnet-bvlc-original-broadcast : Integer = #0B

Section: Tag Encoding

 A context tag carries the tag number in the high nibble, the class bit
 (0x08), and the content length in the low nibble.

  bacnet-object-id-bytes : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  bacnet-object-id-bytes (obj-type) (inst) =
   let v = bit-or (bit-shl obj-type 22) inst
   in [bit-and (bit-shru v 24) 255, bit-and (bit-shru v 16) 255, bit-and (bit-shru v 8) 255, bit-and v 255]

  bacnet-context-object-id : Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  bacnet-context-object-id (tag-num) (obj-type) (inst) =
   [bit-or (bit-or (bit-shl tag-num 4) 8) 4] & bacnet-object-id-bytes obj-type inst

  bacnet-context-unsigned : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  bacnet-context-unsigned (tag-num) (v) =
   let content = if v < 256 then [v] else [bit-and (bit-shru v 8) 255, bit-and v 255]
   in [bit-or (bit-or (bit-shl tag-num 4) 8) (list-length content)] & content

Section: Network and Link Layers

  bacnet-npdu : Integer -> List Integer
  bacnet-npdu (control) = [1, control]

  bacnet-bvlc : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  bacnet-bvlc (function) (payload) =
   let total = 4 + list-length payload
   in [#81, function, bit-and (bit-shru total 8) 255, bit-and total 255] & payload

Section: ReadProperty

 A confirmed request APDU: PDU type 0 with no flags, the max-segments /
 max-response octet (0x05 = up to 1476 bytes), the invoke id, the
 service choice, then the object identifier (context 0) and the
 property identifier (context 1). The NPDU control 0x04 requests a reply.

  bacnet-read-property-apdu : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  bacnet-read-property-apdu (invoke-id) (obj-type) (inst) (prop-id) =
   [0, 5, invoke-id, bacnet-svc-read-property] & bacnet-context-object-id 0 obj-type inst & bacnet-context-unsigned 1 prop-id

  bacnet-build-read-property : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  bacnet-build-read-property (invoke-id) (obj-type) (inst) (prop-id) =
   bacnet-bvlc bacnet-bvlc-original-unicast (bacnet-npdu #04 & bacnet-read-property-apdu invoke-id obj-type inst prop-id)

Section: Application-Tagged Values

 An application-tagged value carries the tag number in the high nibble
 and the length in the low nibble. Unsigned uses tag 2, Real (a 32-bit
 IEEE-754 float, big-endian) uses tag 4, Enumerated uses tag 9.

  bacnet-u32-be : Integer -> List Integer
  bacnet-u32-be (v) =
   [bit-and (bit-shru v 24) 255, bit-and (bit-shru v 16) 255, bit-and (bit-shru v 8) 255, bit-and v 255]

  bacnet-app-unsigned : Integer -> List Integer
  bacnet-app-unsigned (v) =
   if v < 256 then [bit-or (bit-shl 2 4) 1, v]
   else [bit-or (bit-shl 2 4) 2, bit-and (bit-shru v 8) 255, bit-and v 255]

  bacnet-app-enumerated : Integer -> List Integer
  bacnet-app-enumerated (v) = [bit-or (bit-shl 9 4) 1, v]

  bacnet-app-real : Real approximate -> List Integer
  bacnet-app-real (r) =
   [bit-or (bit-shl 4 4) 4] & bacnet-u32-be (real-approx-to-bits r)

Section: WriteProperty

 A WriteProperty request adds the property value, wrapped in an opening
 and closing context tag 3, after the object and property identifiers.
 An opening tag is (tag << 4) | 0x0E, a closing tag (tag << 4) | 0x0F.

  bacnet-open-tag : Integer -> Integer
  bacnet-open-tag (tag-num) = bit-or (bit-shl tag-num 4) #0E

  bacnet-close-tag : Integer -> Integer
  bacnet-close-tag (tag-num) = bit-or (bit-shl tag-num 4) #0F

  bacnet-write-property-apdu : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  bacnet-write-property-apdu (invoke-id) (obj-type) (inst) (prop-id) (value) =
   [0, 5, invoke-id, bacnet-svc-write-property] & bacnet-context-object-id 0 obj-type inst & bacnet-context-unsigned 1 prop-id & [bacnet-open-tag 3] & value & [bacnet-close-tag 3]

  bacnet-build-write-property : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  bacnet-build-write-property (invoke-id) (obj-type) (inst) (prop-id) (value) =
   bacnet-bvlc bacnet-bvlc-original-unicast (bacnet-npdu #04 & bacnet-write-property-apdu invoke-id obj-type inst prop-id value)
